; Entity handler: crusader running along its path script (kind 1 templates, path command 0)
;
; The handler of the crusaders made by the spawner #R$B099 (the slot is a copy of a template of #R$B04C; the slot words
; are described there). Every frame it moves the crusader right by its speed and compares the high byte of x with the
; target coordinate at the path pointer (slot word +4): the path script is a list of pairs (target x in 2-pixel units,
; command), see #R$B218. Until x equals the target the crusader just runs: the hit box test (#R$A851) and the drawing
; with the next animation step go on at #R$B3AD, facing right. When x equals the target (the compare is for equality;
; the speed is below one unit a frame, so it cannot be skipped), the path pointer moves to the next pair and the command
; number is turned into a handler address through the table at #R$B20C, which is written over the handler word of the
; slot: from the next frame the crusader runs a jump (commands 1, 2, 3: #R$B163, #R$B10C, #R$B139), is removed
; (command 4: #R$B08E) or does what command 5 does, and the frame goes on as if there had been no command. Command 0 is
; this handler itself, a command that changes nothing; command 5 is #R$B1CF.
; .
; Slot fields used: +2 word x speed (8.8), +4 word path pointer, +6 word x (8.8, high byte in 2-pixel units), +8 word y;
; the state word +$A is skipped here (it belongs to the jumps); the rest is read by #R$A851, #R$B3AD and #R$A883.
; The path scripts have no terminator: the first two end with command 4 (the crusader is removed), the third with
; command 5, after which the path pointer runs into the code at #R$B236 and the next target x would be the byte $C1 (not
; reached: the cutscene is over by then; read from the code, not run).
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word has been popped)
@label=UpdateCrusader
c$B1D4 POP BC        ; x speed
 $B1D5 POP DE        ; path pointer
 $B1D6 POP HL        ; x (8.8)
 $B1D7 ADD HL,BC     ;
 $B1D8 LD A,(DE)     ; target x of the next path pair
 $B1D9 CP H          ;
 $B1DA JP Z,$B1F3    ; reached: take the command
 $B1DD PUSH HL       ; PUSH then POP: stores x at slot + 6 and leaves SP at slot + 8
 $B1DE POP DE        ; DE = x
@label=UpdateCrusader_Draw
*$B1DF POP HL        ; y (8.8)
 $B1E0 POP BC        ; skip +$A, the jump state
 $B1E1 LD E,H        ; E = y in 2-pixel units
 $B1E2 LD L,H        ; L = y
 $B1E3 LD H,D        ; H = x
 $B1E4 LD A,H        ;
 $B1E5 EX AF,AF'     ; A' = x: its low two bits select the shifted copy
 $B1E6 SRA H         ;
 $B1E8 SRA H         ; x / 4: byte column
 $B1EA LD ($ACD3),HL ; draw command position: (y, x/4)
 $B1ED LD HL,$B3AD   ; the hit test goes on with the sprite description (facing right)
 $B1F0 JP $A851      ; HitTest
